From 72d125312d7e9bbed736f1d26d4e9412bcf378f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <zenithblue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:22:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] panvk/wsi: name the extra_xwayland_image device option

kbase-common/006 passed `kbase_dmabuf && kbase_raw_dri3` positionally
after the designated `.sw_device` initializer.  C fills the next member,
which is `extra_xwayland_image`, so the code did what it meant, but the
field was invisible to readers and would silently change meaning if
wsi_device_options gained a member in between.

Rationale: perf review 2026-10-26 README, correctness items ("unnamed
wsi_device_options field in panvk_wsi.c", package P-C).  The designated
initializer produces the same struct as before, so there is no
behaviour change and no knob.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_wsi.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_wsi.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_wsi.c
index e4850024..56b689c1 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_wsi.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_wsi.c
@@ -532,6 +532,9 @@ panvk_wsi_init(struct panvk_physical_device *physical_device)
                             &instance->drirc.options,
                             &(struct wsi_device_options){
                                .sw_device = uses_kbase && !kbase_dmabuf,
+                               /* Only the raw-FD DRI3 path asks for the
+                                * fourth image when the server is Xwayland. */
+                               .extra_xwayland_image =
                                   kbase_dmabuf && kbase_raw_dri3,
                             });
    if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
-- 
